Third-party material
--------------------
CyberChef (https://github.com/gchq/CyberChef)
  Crown Copyright, licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  Installed as an unmodified npm dependency; its two documented post-install fix
  scripts are executed by scripts/fix-cyberchef.mjs. src/worker.mjs uses CyberChef's
  core Chef and Magic classes. The recipe-URL helpers in src/recipe.mjs and
  public/index.html reproduce the format of CyberChef's Utils.generatePrettyRecipe /
  Utils.encodeURIFragment.

Atomic Red Team (https://github.com/redcanaryco/atomic-red-team)
  Copyright (c) 2018 Red Canary, Inc. MIT License.
  test/corpus/art-commands.json contains command lines extracted from its atomics
  (see test/corpus/extract-art.mjs) and is used only as test plaintext.

CyberChef Recipes (https://github.com/mattnotmax/cyberchef-recipes)
  Not redistributed. test/realworld/benchmark.mjs and test/library/verify-library.mjs
  download it at run time. Recipe-library entries in src/library/recipes.json cite the
  corresponding recipe as their source.

@noble/ciphers (https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-ciphers)
  Copyright (c) Paul Miller. MIT License. Used to pre-check stream-cipher keys
  (ChaCha/Salsa20) and, in tests, to encrypt test data independently of CyberChef.

libphonenumber-js (https://gitlab.com/catamphetamine/libphonenumber-js)
  Copyright (c) Nikolay Kuchumov. MIT License. Installed as an npm dependency to find and
  validate phone numbers in decoded output (metadata from Google's libphonenumber, Apache-2.0).

ThreatLabz ransomware_notes (https://github.com/ThreatLabz/ransomware_notes)
  Copyright (c) 2022 Zscaler ThreatLabz. MIT License. src/ransom/signatures.json contains
  contact points (onion sites, e-mail addresses, Tox IDs) and short lines extracted from these
  notes by scripts/build-ransom-signatures.mjs.

No More Ransom (https://www.nomoreransom.org)
  src/ransom/signatures.json lists the names of the decryptors published on its
  decryption-tools page, with links to that page. No decryptor is redistributed.

@noble/hashes (https://github.com/paulmillr/noble-hashes)
  Copyright (c) Paul Miller. MIT License. Keccak-256 for Ethereum (EIP-55) and Monero checksums.

@zip.js/zip.js (https://github.com/gildas-lormeau/zip.js)
  Copyright (c) Gildas Lormeau. BSD-3-Clause License. Reading zips and Office Open XML files.

Browser edition (web/, built by scripts/build-web.mjs with esbuild, MIT)
  Bundles CyberChef's core and operations (Apache-2.0) and their dependencies, AutoChef, and
  the Node.js compatibility libraries buffer, crypto-browserify (with browserify-aes,
  browserify-des, pbkdf2 …), browserify-zlib/pako, path-browserify, stream-browserify, process,
  events and util (MIT / ISC / Zlib). The licence texts collected from the bundled code are
  shipped next to the bundles as autochef.js.LEGAL.txt and cc-worker.js.LEGAL.txt.

Components under copyleft or dual licences (all are CyberChef dependencies, installed
unmodified from npm and bundled unmodified into web/cc-worker.js)
  openpgp (OpenPGP.js, https://github.com/openpgpjs/openpgpjs) - LGPL-3.0-or-later.
  es6-polyfills (https://github.com/medikoo/es6-polyfills) - LGPL-3.0-or-later.
    Their complete source code is in the npm packages, and scripts/build-web.mjs rebuilds the
    bundle from them, so anyone can replace these libraries with modified versions and rebuild,
    as the LGPL requires. Neither library is modified by AutoChef.
  node-forge (https://github.com/digitalbazaar/forge) - "BSD-3-Clause OR GPL-2.0";
    used under BSD-3-Clause.
  unorm (https://github.com/walling/unorm) - "MIT or GPL-2.0"; used under MIT.
  ua-parser-js (https://github.com/faisalman/ua-parser-js) - pinned to version 1.x
    (package.json "overrides") because it is MIT-licensed; version 2.x is AGPL-3.0 and is not
    used. It provides CyberChef's "Parse User Agent" operation.

MITRE ATT&CK (https://attack.mitre.org)
  test/crypto/families.json lists families and the encryption algorithms named for them
  under technique T1486. © The MITRE Corporation. This work is reproduced and distributed
  with the permission of The MITRE Corporation.

